**assistant**:
> Use `vcat` with splatting to flatten the vectors into one `Vector{Float64}`:
> 
> ```julia
> x = vcat(xx...)
> ```
> 
> Or equivalently:
> 
> ```julia
> x = reduce(vcat, xx)
> ```
> 
> Since all inner vectors appear to have length 5, this gives a vector of length `159 * 5 = 795`.
> 
> If instead you want a `159 × 5` matrix—one original vector per row—use:
> 
> ```julia
> X = reduce(vcat, permutedims.(xx))
> ```
> 
> Or, more efficiently for uniform lengths:
> 
> ```julia
> X = stack(xx; dims=1)
> ```
